# Dual Boot Journey

A long-overdue repo documenting my attempts to dual-boot Linux and Windows on
my PC.

**Update:** this repo originally planned a third dual-boot attempt. That
didn't end up happening. Instead, I got a second laptop from someone for
£50 and installed Arch Linux on it as a standalone system, no dual boot
involved. I've documented that install fully and included it here alongside
the two dual-boot attempts, since it's still part of the same overall
journey into Linux.

This started as my second attempt at proper documentation, after my first two
attempts (Omarchy, then Fedora) both worked, but each came with its own
problems. I had screenshots and notes for both, but assignment submission
week pushed documenting down my priority list. Then a complication with
**Safeblock**, a forensic tool that blocks external drives and forces them
into read-only mode, forced me to reset my PC, and I lost almost all of it.
Only a few photos survive, either shared with a friend or uploaded online.
What Safeblock did exactly is covered later in this repo.

